---
import "@/styles/global.css";
import ExternalArrow from "@/components/ExternalArrow.astro";
import "@/styles/about/exec-application.css";
import Navigation from "@/components/Navigation.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
---

<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8" /><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" /><meta name="description" content="QUT AI & ML Society Executive Applications" /><title>Executive Applications | QUT AI & ML Society</title></head>
  <body class="background-dots"><Navigation />
    <main class="exec-page" data-pagefind-body>
      <section class="exec-hero"><div class="exec-shell"><p>GET INVOLVED</p><h1>Lead what’s<br /><span>next.</span></h1><div><h2>Executive applications</h2><p>The QUT AI &amp; ML Society executive team is responsible for leading the club’s operations, events, and long term direction. Executives work collaboratively to plan initiatives, deliver high quality events, support members’ learning and professional development, and ensure the club operates sustainably and in line with university requirements.</p></div></div></section>
      <section class="exec-section"><div class="exec-shell"><div class="exec-heading"><p>THE ANNUAL CYCLE</p><h2>When applications<br /><span>open.</span></h2></div><article class="exec-timing"><b>01</b><div><h3>Annual General Meeting</h3><p>Executive applications open once per year at the club’s Annual General Meeting. Every executive position is declared vacant and open for re election at the AGM.</p></div><div><h3>Put your hand up</h3><p>Any eligible member may nominate for a role, and applicants can outline their interest, experience, and vision for the position before voting takes place.</p></div></article></div></section>
      <section class="exec-section exec-roles"><div class="exec-shell"><div class="exec-heading"><p>WHAT THE ROLE INVOLVES</p><h2>Bring your<br /><span>contribution.</span></h2></div><div class="exec-role-layout"><p>QUT AIML Executives are expected to actively contribute to the club by attending events and meetings, taking ownership of their role, and representing the society professionally. Each role has defined responsibilities and weekly time commitments, which may increase near major events.</p><aside><span>ELIGIBILITY</span><p>Members need to continue their studies at QUT the following year.</p><a href="https://github.com/QUT-AIML/Constitution/blob/main/Role-Descriptions.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View role descriptions <ExternalArrow /></a></aside></div></div></section>
    </main><Footer />
  </body>
</html>
